' ============================================================
' Sensitivity analysis for an EPD
'
' Varies the main A1 and A3 parameters up and down, one at a time,
' and shows how far each one moves the results of the EPD method.
'
' A parameter here is a variable used as an amount in a PROCESS
' block, for example:
'
'     LET cement_mass = 300
'     ...
'     INPUT USE PROCESS "BRIDGE | Cement | kg", cement_mass, kg
'
' SHOW SYSTEM "A1: Raw material supply" PARAMS lists the parameters
' of a module's product system.
'
' DECIDE: the system names (the module totals), the parameters, and
' the range. BY has no default.
' ============================================================

LET range_percent = 10

' A1: the main raw material amounts
' SENSITIVITY ON "A1: Raw material supply" USING "EN15804+A2 (EF 3.1)" BY 10%
'   VARY cement_mass, aggregate_mass
'   SAVE "sensitivity_a1.csv"
' END SENSITIVITY

' A3: energy and yield in manufacturing
' SENSITIVITY ON "A3: Manufacturing" USING "EN15804+A2 (EF 3.1)" BY 10%
'   VARY electricity_kwh, heat_mj
'   SAVE "sensitivity_a3.csv"
' END SENSITIVITY

' The whole EPD at once: groups of parameters that move together,
' summed over modules A to C, with module D shown on its own. It needs
' the EPD block and EPD CALCULATE earlier in the same session. Only the
' modules that hold a parameter of a group are calculated again.
' EPD SENSITIVITY BY 20% SAVE "sensitivity_epd.csv"
'   GROUP "Electricity" VARY electricity_kwh
'   GROUP "Raw materials" VARY cement_mass, aggregate_mass
' END EPD SENSITIVITY

PRINT "Take the apostrophes off the SENSITIVITY blocks and put your own names in."
